- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests`

**How to implement.** `MaterialEntry.complexity` becomes mandatory, and `properties` becomes a member computed from it (001 §B; .spec-md §0.1 'MaterialLibrary.fs' row, §3.2). After steps 10 and 11 every construction already sets `properties = complexity.toProperties` with a present complexity. The record and all its consumers change in this one step, so the build stays green. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs:MaterialEntry`: the field `properties` is deleted, and `complexity : MaterialComplexity` replaces the option. The record gains `member this.properties : OpticalPropertiesWithDisp = this.complexity.toProperties`, so its readers (`resolveMaterialWithDisp`, `MaterialEntry.dispersion`, `Propagation.fs`, the views and the tests) keep compiling unchanged. Its doc says the complexity is the entry's physics and `properties` its engine composition. `builtInEntries` drops each `properties = …` line and each `Some`. Every field is now data, so `MaterialEntry` gains F#'s structural equality. (2) Every other construction drops `properties = …` and `Some`: `OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs` (`entryFromTabulated`, `entryOfAxis`), `OpticalConstructor.Storage/Report.fs` `dtoToEntry` and `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorView.fs` `entryUnder` (`:416-424`). So do the fixtures: `LibraryFacetsTests.fs` `materialEntryWith`, the dispersive fixture of `OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs`, `OutOfBandBadgeTests.fs` `dispersiveMaterial` (`:64-72`), the minted-id fact of `DispersionModelsTests.fs`, `FsxAcceptanceTests.fs` `material` and the step-10 fact of `MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs`. The copy-and-updates `MaterialProxyTests.fs:52` and `SampleProxyTests.fs:487` keep only `complexity = …`. (3) Every reader of the option reads the value, and every `None` arm that stood for a coded, view-only preset is deleted with nothing replacing it. `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialStore.fs`: `payloadOf` (`:76-80`) is `VersionPayload<MaterialComplexity, MaterialMetadata>` and compares the complexity directly, and the `MaterialMetadata` doc (`:28-34`) drops its coded-preset sentences. `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs`: the four private entry members (`constantEpsOpt`, `dispersiveEpsOpt`, `activeOpt`, `magneticOpt`) and the anisotropy facet read `entry.complexity`, and the anisotropy doc's defensive-`None` sentence goes. `OpticalConstructor.Domain/OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs:84-90`: `ofEntry` is `ReachableMaterial.definedSegmentsOf entry.complexity`. `OpticalConstructor.Ui/NkDispersionChart.fs`: `previewAnisotropy` (`:101-110`) is deleted, and its callers `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs:1114` and `:1151` read `shownEntry.complexity.anisotropy`. The docs that describe the coded-preset fallback or name `previewAnisotropy` (`NkDispersionChart.fs:156-163`, `:170-175`, `:208-211`; `MaterialEditorView.fs:266-270`) are rewritten: every component is drawn when a complexity names no gyration class. `MaterialsWindowView.fs`: `editableSelection` (`:253-264`) and the view panel's editability (`:1115-1120`) read `isEditable` off the complexity, and the caption ` (view-only engine preset)` becomes ` (view-only)`. `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:MaterialComplexity.isEditable`: its doc no longer contrasts the gate with complexity presence. (4) `MaterialEditorView.fs`: the view-only case carries the complexity it shows, `ViewOnlyMaterial of reason : ControlCaption * shown : MaterialComplexity` (`:64-69`). The fields `presetProperties` and `viewOnlyComplexity` (`:147-152`) are deleted. `previewProperties`, `previewGyrationComponents` and `previewMuKind` (`:256-290`) read `shown`, so their `None` arms go. `initMaterialEditor` (`:321-387`) seeds an editable entry through `ofComplexity`, whose `Error e` gives `ViewOnlyMaterial (e.caption, entry.complexity)`. Any other entry opens as `ViewOnlyMaterial (ControlCaption "this entry's physics is not editable term data — view-only", entry.complexity)`. The binders at `:411` and `:1289` take `(reason, _)`, and `complexitySummary`'s view-only caption (`:295`) becomes `view-only`. The module doc (`:1-20`), the `EditorMode` doc (`:64-66`) and the inline comments (`:360-363`, `:373-375`) describe the view-only case as a complexity that is not editable term data, and so does `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorWindow.fs:12-19`. (5) Test readers follow: `MaterialComplexityTests.fs` `AC-B7 every re-expressed built-in's toProperties reproduces the original preset at reference wavelengths`; `MaterialImportTests.fs` `assertEditableDispersive`, `formula 2 segment carries the page's wavelength_range in µm` and the facts S1.1 steps 1 and 2 added, which now match the record itself; `LibraryFacetsTests.fs` `anisotropyOf reads the re-seeded coded presets from data`; and `OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs` `a coded-preset material (spectrum-spanning band) never flags`, which drops its option match and its comment's former-`None` clause. In `MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs`, `ofComplexity round-trips the editable built-ins value-identically through toComplexity`, `init seeds a new material, an existing editable entry, and a view-only entry` and the two Save facts read the value. (6) Two facts lose their subject and are deleted. `every built-in carries Some complexity after the step-004 re-seed` (`MaterialComplexityTests.fs:132-148`) is now guaranteed by the type. `spec 0040 006: a coded preset with no stored tree still renders all components` (`MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs:1053-1064`) needs an entry without a complexity, which no longer exists; the view-only class restriction stays covered by `spec 0040 006: a view-only entry reads the class off its stored complexity tree — Langasite carries g₁₁ / g₃₃`. Three facts are renamed because their names state the option: `Save adds a NEW material with complexity Some, updates an EXISTING one, and Cancel writes nothing` becomes `Save adds a NEW material with its complexity, updates an EXISTING one, and Cancel writes nothing`; `acceptance: Save round-trips a NEW entry through MaterialProxy with complexity Some` becomes `acceptance: Save round-trips a NEW entry through MaterialProxy with its complexity`; and `a complexity-less entry opens view-only with no Save affordance and no ladder` becomes `a non-editable entry opens view-only with no Save affordance and no ladder`. (7) In every file this step edits, each comment and failure message that says `complexity = None`, `complexity = Some` or `Some complexity` is rewritten or deleted.

**Acceptance.** After `complexity` becomes mandatory, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, one fact fewer for the deleted MaterialComplexityTests fact; ui-tests (MaterialEditorWindowTests, MaterialsWindowTests, NkDispersionChartTests, OutOfBandBadgeTests, FsxAcceptanceTests) MUST pass, one fact fewer for the deleted coded-preset fact and with the renamed Save fact; ui-smoke MUST pass with the two renamed facts; and build, elevation and the four s02 invariants MUST pass.
